   "text": {
    "L1": "A river begins at its source, high up in hills or mountains.",
    "L2": "Water flows downhill, so the river travels from high land to lower land.",
    "L3": "In the mountains, the river is narrow and fast, and it cuts valleys.",
    "L4": "In the plains, it slows down, spreads out, and drops fine soil called silt.",
    "L5": "A smaller river that joins the main river is called a tributary.",
    "L6": "Tributaries make the main river bigger as it continues its journey.",
    "L7": "People settle near rivers for water, farming, fishing, and travel.",
    "L8": "The river ends at its mouth, where it meets a sea, lake, or bigger river."
   },
